From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:30:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 72/72] macos: hotty layers are Core Animation layers over the
 terminal's

Each hotty layer is a CALayer, clipped to its placement, whose contents
is an sRGB IOSurface the window server composites with the terminal's. A
change writes only the rectangles that changed into an IOSurface the
window server is not reading (IOSurfaceIsInUse), brought up to date from
the newest first, and draws no terminal frame. Where the layers show
goes with the terminal frame's IOSurface, and the main thread lays them
out as it shows that IOSurface, in the same transaction.
